Post Date: 2017-06-06T19:07:33Z
Current Date: April 4 2025
Title: Execute specific (automatic) actions when the client un/subscribe to Flowable.
Description: I was trying to create a `Flowable` that is connected to a source when the client subscribes, and disconnect from the source when the client unsubscribes.

I tried first using a custom `Flowable`, in this way:

```
public final class SensorEventFlowable extends Flowable<RxSensorEvent> {

    private final SensorManager sensorManager;
    private final Sensor sensor;
    private final int samplingPeriodUs;

    SensorEventFlowable(SensorManager sensorManager, Sensor sensor, int samplingPeriodUs) {
        this.sensorManager = sensorManager;
        this.sensor = sensor;
        this.samplingPeriodUs = samplingPeriodUs;
    }

    @Override
    protected void subscribeActual(Subscriber<? super RxSensorEvent> subscriber) {
        Listener listener = new Listener(sensorManager, subscriber);
        subscriber.onSubscribe(listener);
        sensorManager.registerListener(listener, sensor, samplingPeriodUs);
    }

    static final class Listener implements Subscription, SensorEventListener {
        private final SensorManager sensorManager;
        private final Subscriber<? super RxSensorEvent> subscriber;

        Listener(SensorManager sensorManager, Subscriber<? super RxSensorEvent> subscriber) {
            this.sensorManager = sensorManager;
            this.subscriber = subscriber;
        }

        @Override
        public void onSensorChanged(SensorEvent event) {
            subscriber.onNext(new RxSensorEvent(event));
        }

        @Override
        public void request(long n) { }

        @Override
        public void cancel() {
            sensorManager.unregisterListener(this);
        }
    }
}
```


but I was suggested to use `Flowable.create()` instead. So I tried to use it:

```
public final class SensorEventFlowableFactory {

    public static Flowable<RxSensorEvent> create(SensorManager sensorManager, Sensor sensor, int samplingPeriodUs) {
        return Flowable.create(e -> {
            Listener listener = new Listener(e);
            sensorManager.registerListener(listener, sensor, samplingPeriodUs);
        }, BackpressureStrategy.MISSING);
    }

    static final class Listener implements SensorEventListener {
        private final FlowableEmitter<RxSensorEvent> emitter;

        Listener(FlowableEmitter<RxSensorEvent> emitter) {
            this.emitter = emitter;
        }

        @Override
        public void onSensorChanged(SensorEvent event) {
            emitter.onNext(new RxSensorEvent(event));
        }
    }
}

```

I have some doubts about this code:

1. In the first implementation I have `cancel` method that will execute `sensorManager.unregisterListener(this);`. How can I make this happens in the second implementation? (when the client unsubscribe from the flowable). I don't want the client to be aware about this.

2. Actually, if I am not wrong, the method `sensorManager.registerListener(listener, sensor, samplingPeriodUs);` is called when the Flowable is created, and not when the client subscribe. Is that correct? If so, where do I need to place that call (registerListner) in order to be executed only if and when the client subscribes?

